Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Check if the system is EFI
Description Task 1: Check if the system is using EFI firmware by looking at the /sys/firmware/efi/efivars directory.

Task 2: Remove the grub.cfg file if the system is EFI
Description Task 2: Delete the grub.cfg file from /boot/grub2/ if the system is detected as EFI-based.

Task 3: Install a user template for GRUB
Description Task 3: Install a user-defined template file for GRUB under /etc/grub.d/01_users, ensuring it is owned by root and has a mode of 0700, and trigger an update of GRUB.

Task 4: Add a password to the EFI GRUB configuration
Description Task 4: Insert a line to enable a password for GRUB in the EFI configuration file /etc/grub2-efi.cfg, and notify the GRUB update handler.

Task 5: Add a password to the MBR GRUB configuration
Description Task 5: Insert a line to enable a password for GRUB in the MBR configuration file /etc/grub2.cfg, and notify the GRUB update handler.

Task 6: Add --unrestricted option to specified files
Description Task 6: Replace occurrences of CLASS="..." with CLASS="... --unrestricted" in files specified by the variable grub_password_unrestricted_files if the variable grub_password_unrestricted is set to true, and notify the GRUB update handler.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Check if the system is EFI
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars
    state: directory
    path_type: inode
  register: efi_system
  changed_when: false

- name: Remove the grub.cfg file if the system is EFI
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: /boot/grub2/grub.cfg
    state: absent
  when: efi_system.stat.isdir

- name: Install a user template for GRUB
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    src: templates/grub_user_template
    dest: /etc/grub.d/01_users
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0700'
  notify: update_grub

- name: Add a password to the EFI GRUB configuration
  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:
    path: /etc/grub2-efi.cfg
    regexp: '^set superusers="root"'
    line: 'set superusers="root"\npassword_pbkdf2 root'
  notify: update_grub

- name: Add a password to the MBR GRUB configuration
  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:
    path: /etc/grub2.cfg
    regexp: '^set superusers="root"'
    line: 'set superusers="root"\npassword_pbkdf2 root'
  notify: update_grub

- name: Add --unrestricted option to specified files
  ansible.builtin.replace:
    path: "{{ item }}"
    regexp: 'CLASS="'
    replace: 'CLASS="--unrestricted"'
  loop: "{{ grub_password_unrestricted_files }}"
  when: grub_password_unrestricted | bool
  notify: update_grub

